 "rulebook": "FIBA Official Basketball Rules 2024: Art. 2 (court), Art. 3 and the Basketball Equipment appendix (size-7 ball), Art. 13 (how the ball is played), Art. 23 (out of bounds), Art. 24 (dribbling), Art. 25 (travelling), Art. 28.1.3 (when a dribbled ball is in the frontcourt)",
 "deviations": [
  "Art. 3 (equipment): the hand holds the ball by a grip switched on and off, not by fingers; the ball is released when the grip is switched off, and after that release no grip takes it again.",
  "Art. 24.1.2 (the ball 'comes to rest' in a hand) is read as: a hand's touch of the ball that lasts longer than 0.3 s. A dribble that has ended cannot legally be started again (Art. 24.2), so a ball that comes to rest in a hand, or is touched by both hands at once, ends the attempt.",
  "Art. 13: every touch of the ball by a part of you other than a hand is a violation; intent (an accidental touch of a leg is legal in the rule book) cannot be judged.",
  "Art. 14 / 24 give no distance for 'control' of a dribbled ball: here the ball's centre must stay within 2.0 m (horizontally) of your pelvis, so that a ball thrown ahead and walked after is not a dribble.",
  "Art. 28 (eight seconds to reach the frontcourt) is not applied: the attempt lasts at most 60 s of robot time."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Dribble the basketball in your right hand from the end line across the centre line, 14 m up the court, without a dribbling or a travelling violation.",
  "rules": "A FIBA court, 28.0 m by 15.0 m inside its boundary lines (lines 0.05 m wide); the centre line's axis is 14.0 m from the end line. The ball is a size-7 basketball (0.239 m across, 0.62 kg, it keeps 0.85 of its speed in a bounce on the floor). It starts gripped in your right hand, and you stand still. Starting the dribble: the first foot you lift makes the other your pivot foot; the pivot foot, and before a foot is lifted either foot, may not slide more than 0.2 m along the floor, and the pivot foot may not leave the floor before you have let go of the ball (a foot has left the floor when it has not touched it for 0.03 s). The dribble: after the release you play the ball with one hand at a time, by touches that push it to the floor (thrown, tapped, rolled or bounced): between two touches by your hands the ball must have touched the floor; contacts of a hand less than 0.03 s apart are one touch; the release counts as the first touch (the releasing hand may stay on the ball for 0.03 s after the grip opens; the next touch by a hand needs a bounce on the floor first); no grip takes the ball again. There is no limit to your steps while the ball is not in a hand. You succeed at the first moment the ball touches the floor in the frontcourt (beyond the centre line's far edge, 14.0 m plus half a line width from the end line) with both your feet in the frontcourt (every point where each foot last touched the floor is beyond that edge), after at least one touch of your dribble. You fail if you travel at the start; if a hand's touch lasts longer than 0.3 s (the ball has come to rest in the hand); if both hands touch the ball at the same time; if a hand touches the ball twice without the ball having touched the floor in between; if the ball touches any part of you other than a hand; if the ball's centre is ever more than 2.0 m (horizontally) from your pelvis after the release; if the ball or any part of you touches the floor on or outside a boundary line (out of bounds); if you fall (a fall: your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than your feet on the floor); or after 60 s.",
  "venue": "You stand in the backcourt just inside the end line, facing up the court (+x): the end line's inner edge is 0.5 m behind your pelvis and the centre line 14.0 m beyond that edge. The basket of this end is to your right: the court's long axis, with the backboard (its lower edge 2.9 m high, 1.2 m in from the end line) and the ring, is 2.5 m to your right; the side lines are 15.0 m apart, the nearer one 5 m to your left. Painted on the floor: the boundary lines, the restricted area, the free-throw line (5.8 m from the end line) and circle, the three-point line, the centre line and circle. The ball is against the end of your right fist. A ball is released when the hand's grip is switched off.",
  "difficulty": "The ball keeps 85 % of its speed in a bounce, so every touch has to push it down and forward again to where the hand will be, with a rigid palm 8 cm wide, for 14 m, on a body whose walking gait covers about 0.7 m/s, drifts in heading, and is disturbed by every push of the arm. The built-in walking gait steps on the spot even at a zero command, so while the ball is in your hand its steps are counted like any others."
 },
